#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A verse on the glass, every fifteen minutes.

Caleb, 2026-10-16: "Add hourly verses to the hud popping up", then "Make them
stay until I x them out, also make it every 15 min". The daemon runs this every
900 s, and each run puts one verse at the top of the screen. It stays until he
closes it, and the next run replaces the card in place rather than stacking.
Nothing is drawn from 2am to 8am. Double-clicking the card opens the HUD's
chat already asking about that verse (the Screen's `ask=`).

The verses walk in order, one per quarter hour since the epoch, so two runs in
the same quarter show the same verse, and there are more verses than waking
quarters so a day never repeats one. The list leans on the
victory of Jesus and on contentment in Him, the two things his grandfather and
Joel George keep pointing him back to (second-brain domains/faith.md, people.md).
KJV, because it is public domain and every line here can be checked against it.

Usage:
    hud-verse            put this quarter hour's verse up (nothing 2am to 8am)
    hud-verse --now      put it up even in quiet hours
    hud-verse --dry-run  print what it would draw
    hud-verse --list     every verse, in order
"""

